essor efficiency up by 30% I'll  say it should all balance out in fact it  turns out that the s6 is battery  performance is just a hair under the  iPhone 6 plus except for music playback  all right let's move on to the camera  the camera is definitely a story of  refinement 16 megapixels on the rear 5  megapixels on the front both with an  f-stop of 1.9 which means more exposure  60% brighter on the front and 34%  brighter on the rear to be exact the  camera also loads up in the background  whenever the phone is awake so it  launches faster  there's also faster autofocus and  autofocus tracking optical image  stabilization makes return and  absolutely brilliant in the night for  said potential s6 buyers will be happy  about that one but unfortunately when it  comes to the UI it seems that Samsung  has shamelessly stolen some ideas from  HTC okay let's move on to the design as  they say beauty is in the eye of the  beholder and many be holders out there  find this phone beautiful but I'm not  actually whole heartedly one of them  unfortunately for me at the front and  the sides of the device look great  although the top and bottom bezels could  be a bit smaller for a more attractive  proportion and I think the design  language in regards of the trims of the  phones does seem to have a slightly  bulbous nature and when you flip the  phone around at the unsymmetrical  fingerprint scanner in combination with  that camera mount design just doesn't  sit right with me but that's just my  opinion though Gorilla Glass 4 back  panels refreshing but may be of some  concern to those who aren't a fan of  phone cases because you know we've all  seen the smash backs of the Nexus floor  or iPhone 5 and 5s --is ok so there's  been a fair few changes to the design  that this has come at a cost there are  two main trade-offs to this new design  and it may annoy some people out there  number one waterproofing and water  resistance has now gone from the phone  and number two there's no removable  battery or SD card storage anymore for  some smartphone enthusiasts these issues  could make or break your purchase but  for the general public mainly they is  coming from an iPhone or phones with  shielding batteries will probably not  mine too much one other gripe that I  have with the design of the device is  the bottom although it looks good I'm  somewhat disappointed by Samsung's lack  of creativity here because really  there's a y plethora of design  combinations that you could use for the  bottom of any phone but this clearly is  borrowing from the iPhone 6s design  language some people out there may not  care but I'm just not too keen on it  I think Samsung should be more like HTC  in this regard finding their own unique  design groove making it so good that  other people want to copy from you and  not the other way around  but to Samsung's credit the s6 edge is  pretty unique I'm glad that fixed on the  design issues with the edge edition  namely that the edge runs along both  sides of the device and I could just  imagine how natural will feel to swipe  in from the side of an app whose UI  demands that kind of motion the facedown  notifications are pretty cool as well so  you get a subtle indication of when  someone is trying to contact you  Samsung is also built certain software  around this like tickers alarm clocks  and something called people edge where  you can pull up your favorite  color-coded contacts with a swipe from  the edge of the screen and I might also  add that the price point this time is  correct having this the same price of  the regular s6 actually makes sense this  time now this means that it's a  variation of the s6 and not somewhat of  a different premium range the price  point was an issue that had me rather  reserved about the note for edge so in  conclusion  despite some design quirks my initial  thoughts and the s6 and s6 edge are  mostly positive and if you're out there  and you don't mind giving up a bit of  graphics performance for a very high  screen resolution and are a fan of the  design I definitely think the s6 and s6  edge would be worth a look it's probably  a worthy upgrade for someone who has an  s4 but for s5 owners or Note 4 owners I  think these guys will still get a lot of  extra mileage out of their phones as for  me I am personally happy with my note 4  and don't really see a reason to change  to an s6 but who knows when the phone  comes to stores in Australia I go in  have a quick play and see what I think  about it anyway thanks for watching  hopefully this video has been quite  informational for you and you've found  some extra things that were useful to  you and if you have don't forget to  share it along to someone who'll be  interested give it a thumbs up write a  comment and subscribe thanks for  watching guys I'll see you again soon  for the next video  Cheers
 

